                // f003_the_gate_is_a_hole_in_the_wall_and_not_two_towers_beside_it` is the
                // rule that keeps them gone: **a mass that stands on the wall line may not
                // reach further out than the wall's widest course.** A LEDGE may, and must.
                //
                // The opening itself is unchanged and is not built here — it is the gap the
                // courses above leave at `x = -14..14`, `y = 0..20`, and
                // `scripts/f003-ashgate.txt` ACT 1 measures it by being dropped into it.
                // What is built here is the **frame**, and it is three elements:
