                //     plinth line (22.50 m off the centre) while the wall behind them batters
                //     back from 21.97 to 14.53. So the pier steps 0.53 m out of the face at
                //     the bottom and 7.97 m at the top: the gate is read from the ground as
                //     two vertical piers interrupting a battered wall, which is the shape in
                //     the reference. **They are not towers** — they end at the coping, they
                //     never leave the plinth line, and the rule above holds for them.
