                // ---- The cornice ladder — 30 / 60 / 90 m, and it is what you swing from
                // ⭐ **The property the deleted gantry crossbeams were carrying, moved onto
                // the wall.** `maps.ron` argued the gantry as physics and the argument is
                // still the right one: *"the bottom of the pendulum lies vertically under the
                // ANCHOR — on a solid tower that point is inside the tower."* So the wall
                // needs ledges that hang out over air, and until 2026-08-29 it had exactly
                // two of them (the 60 m gallery and the 120 m crown corbel), 60 m apart.
                //
                // ## The one number the whole ladder is designed against: **22.50 m**
                //
                // The wall is battered — `base_thickness_m` 45.0 down to `top_thickness_m`
                // 28.0 — so the PLINTH is the widest thing a plumb line can meet on the way
                // down, and it stands 22.50 m off the centre line. **A ledge is worth hooking
                // iff its outer edge reaches past 22.50.** Every course below stops at
                // exactly **26.00 m**: 3.50 m of free strip, which is five body widths
                // (`game.ron: player.radius_m` 0.35). `tests/world.rs::
                // f003_every_cornice_on_the_wall_hangs_over_open_ground` measures that strip
                // for every ledge on all four runs and fails under 4 x the radius.
                //
                // ## Why 30 / 60 / 90 and not one per 15 m course joint
                //
                // 35 m was the pitch of the deleted lane and `FIND-041`'s rule is
                // `bottom = H - L` with a swing only while `d < H`. A 30 m spacing is inside
                // that everywhere, and the ladder then reads ground -> 30 -> 60 -> 90 -> 120,
                // one hook per rung, with the 60 m gallery and the 120 m crown as the two
                // rungs that were already there. Seven rungs would have been prettier and
                // would have put four more slabs in the sightline between the gallery and
                // the crown corbel, which is a 6-degree window already (`FIND-126`).
                //
                // Each course is 2 m thick, seated **1.50 m into the band it sits on** so it
                // cannot float off a battered face, and runs the FULL length of its wall on
                // BOTH faces — a wall with a ledge on one side only is a lie about the wall.
                // The three depths are therefore different (6.60 / 8.72 / 10.84 m): the face
                // behind them steps back 1.06 m per 15 m course and the outer edge does not.
                // Colour `sand_brown` — the same key the 60 m gallery and the crown corbels
                // already wear, which is this map's word for "an anchorable ledge".
