                // ---- The gantry line is GONE, and this is where it stood ---------------
                // Fourteen stations of two 8 x 56 x 8 m columns and a 44 x 4 x 8 m crossbeam
                // at 60 m, at a 35 m pitch from z = 227.5 to -262.5 down the main street.
                // A torii. **The user, 2026-08-29, having played it:** *„aktuell sind
                // immernoch die grossen tuerme /gates beim eingang. das passt GAR nicht zu
                // attack on titan und existiert so nicht!"* — 14 of the 36 things hanging
                // over the main street were carried by nothing but their own columns
                // (`tests/world.rs::
                // f003_nothing_freestanding_spans_the_main_street_the_way_a_gate_would`,
                // which counted them before this line was written).
                //
                // ⚠️ **THEY WERE CARRYING A MECHANIC AND IT DID NOT GO WITH THEM.** The file
                // argued them, correctly, as physics: *"The bottom of the pendulum lies
                // vertically under the ANCHOR. On a solid tower that point is inside the
                // tower, so a swing that is allowed to run its course ends in the wall you
                // are hanging from. Two columns and a crossbeam put the anchor over open
                // ground."* That property now lives on the wall: the **cornice ladder** at
                // 30 / 60 / 90 m on every face of every run, and the **gate cornice** over
                // the road at 34 m. `f003_every_cornice_on_the_wall_hangs_over_open_ground`
                // is that sentence as an assert, and `scripts/f003-wall.txt` ACT 2 flies it.
                //
                // 🔴 **AND WHAT IT COST IS NOT PAID BACK HERE, so read this before believing
                // the district still swings.** The wall stands at z = -120; the gantry lane
                // ran 315 m of main street from z = 227.5 to -87.5, and no cornice on a wall
                // reaches that. Inside the district what is left over open ground is the
                // eight 35 m bell towers, the church, and the roofs — and `FIND-058` measured
                // a roof-to-roof hop across a 7 m street at 18.9 m/s against the lane's 31.4.
                // **The main street north of the wall is a hop lane now, not a swing lane**
                // (`docs/FINDINGS.md` FIND-215, `docs/QUESTIONS.md` Q-083: what replaces it is
                // his call, and „adde andere tuerme beim wasser" is already his answer for the
                // canal). Whoever puts a spine back over this street builds it out of the
                // town — a bell tower every 35 m, an arcade, a viaduct — and not out of a
                // freestanding crossbeam.

